(7517833, 1199764, 104230, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SaraR:</b></div><hr/><i> What an amazing catch.  The only time I have seen a hawk actually in my garden, he was in the process of killing a starling.... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Robert was discreet and did not mention that the first time we saw this fine fellow he was atop one of our fence posts with a small rabbit pinned firmly under his talons.  He stayed there until he had torn it apart and eaten everything but the bones.  On the plus side our garden is thriving with fewer rabbits ...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2017-06-11 13:14:33.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by SaraR: What an amazing catch.  The only time I have seen a hawk actually in my garden, he was in the process of killing a starling....  Robert was discreet and did not mention that the first time we saw this fine fellow he was atop one of our fence posts with a small rabbit pinned firmly under his talons.  He stayed there until he had torn it apart and eaten everything but the bones.  On the plus side our garden is thriving with fewer rabbits ...', '2017-06-08 10:06:56.000000', '2017-06-11 14:14:33.000000', 0),
